# An install that stops halfway (a power cut; here the test flag
# installstop=N) leaves a disk without a partition table, which `install`
# recognises and can do again. Nothing half-valid is ever on the disk.
@sata
@blank-disk 64
@install-medium
@args installstop=2
$& install sata0
> yes
$wait
~ ^install failed: stopped after step 2 for a test
The disk has no partition table now; 'install sata0' starts over.
$ install
~ ^  sata0 +64 MiB  "QEMU HARDDISK": an install that was not finished$
~ would install again
@reboot
~ not BeeFS, left untouched
$ install
~ an install that was not finished
